# RTK Token Reduction (ECI)

This repo uses RTK (Rust Token Killer) to cut LLM token consumption 60-90% on terminal command output. Verbose CLI output (passing tests, git boilerplate, directory noise) wastes context budget that should go to reasoning.

## Terminal commands

- If the RTK hook is installed, commands are rewritten automatically — run them normally.
- **Native Windows:** auto-rewrite hook is unavailable — always prefix commands with `rtk` (see below).
- If output looks raw/verbose (hook absent or Windows native), prefix explicitly: `rtk git status`, `rtk git diff`, `rtk grep <pattern> .`, `rtk find <path>`, `rtk ls`, `rtk read <file>`.
- Tests: run via `rtk test <command>` (or `rtk jest` / `rtk vitest` / `rtk pytest`) — failures only.
- Unknown/uncovered commands with long output: `rtk err <cmd>` (errors only) or `rtk summary <cmd>`.

## When detail is missing

- After a **failed** command, RTK prints a tee log path — read that file instead of re-running (Linux/macOS/WSL: `~/.local/share/rtk/tee/`; Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\rtk\tee\`).
- Need raw output once: `RTK_DISABLED=1 <command>`. Never suggest uninstalling RTK to work around one command.

## Read/Grep/Glob bypass (structural)

The hook covers shell/Bash tool calls only — built-in Read/Grep/Glob and MCP outputs are NOT filtered. Prefer shell `rg` / `cat` / `find` or `rtk read` / `rtk grep` / `rtk find` so output is compacted and counted toward savings. Project-local filters in `.rtk/filters.toml` require `rtk trust` once after cloning (0.43.x security gate).

## Output hygiene

Do not paste large raw command output into chat or files; reference the filtered summary or the tee log path. Repo-specific filter overrides live in `.rtk/filters.toml`.

For savings reports, troubleshooting, or writing custom filters, see the `rtk-operations` rule.
